ACT XX OF 2010
PEOPLES UNIVERSITY OF MEDICAL
AND HEALTH
SCIENCES FOR WOMEN, SHAHEED BENAZIRABAD,
ACT, 2009
An Act to establish a University known as the Peoples
University of Medical and Health Sciences for
Women at Shaheed Benazirabad.
[Gazette of Sindh,
Extraordinary,
12th November, 2010]
No.PAS/Legis-B-24/2009, dated 12-11-2010.---The
Peoples University of Medical and Health Sciences for Women, Shaheed Benazirabad Bill, 2009
having been passed by the Provincial Assembly of Sindh
on 21st December, 2009 and assented to by the Governor of Sindh
on 10th November, 2010 is hereby published as an Act of the Legislature of Sindh.
Preamble.---Whereas
it is expedient to establish a University known as the Peoples University of
Medical and Health Sciences for Women at Shaheed Benazirabad, and to provide for matters ancillary thereto;
It is hereby enacted as follows:--
CHAPTER-1
PRELIMINARY
2. Definitions. In this Act, unless
there is anything repugnant in the subject or context-
(i) "Academic
Council" means the Academic Council of the University;
(ii) "affiliated
college" means the college affiliated to the University but not maintained
or administered by it;
(iii) "affiliated
institute" means an institute affiliated to the University but not
maintained or administered by it;
(iv) "Authority" means any of the
authorities of the University specified in section 20;
(v) "Chairperson" means the Chairperson
of a Teaching Department;
(vi) "Chancellor" means the Chancellor of
the University;
(vii) "college"
means a constituent college or affiliated college imparting instructions or
practical training in courses of studies relating to health sciences and allied
sciences;
(viii) "constituent
college" means a college maintained and administered by the University;
(ix) "constituent
institute" means an institute maintained and administered by the
University;
(x) "Commission" means the Higher
Education Commission;
(xi) "Dean" means the head of a faculty;
(xii) "Director" means the head of an
Institute;
(xiii) "Faculty" means a faculty of the
University;
(xiv) "Government" means the Government of Sindh;
(xv) "Honorary Professor" means a
Professor who provides academic service on honorary basis;
(xvi) "Medical
College" means Peoples Medical
College, Shaheed Benazirabad;
(xvii)
"Officer" means any of the officers of the University specified in
section 9;
(xviii) "prescribed" means prescribed by statutes, regulations
or rules;
(xix)
"Principal" means the head of a constituent or affiliated college;
(xx)
"Pro-Chancellor" means the Pro-Chancellor of the University;
(xxi)
"Professor Emeritus" means a retired Professor working in the
University;
(xxii)
"Pro-Vice Chancellor" means the Pro-Vice Chancellor of the
University;
(xxiii) "registered graduate" means a graduate of the University
who has his name entered in the register maintained for the purpose;
(xxiv)
"Registrar" means the Registrar of the University;
(xxv)
"Schedule" means a Schedule to this Act;
(xxvi)
"Senate" means the Senate of the University;
(xxvii) "statutes, regulations and rules" means respectively the
statutes, regulations and rules made under this Act;
(xxviii)
"Syndicate" means the Syndicate of the University;
(xxix)
"teachers" means teacher engaged as Professor, Associate Professor,
Assistant Professor, Senior Registrar and Lecturer and such other persons as
may be declared to be the teachers;
(xxx)
"Teaching Department" means a Teaching Department established and
maintained or recognized by the University;
(xxxi)
"University" means the Peoples University of Medical and Health
Sciences for Women Shaheed Benazirabad;
(xxxii)
"Vice-Chancellor" means the Vice-Chancellor of the University; and
(xxxiii)
"visiting teacher" means a teacher, who is
invited for teaching by the University for a short period.

